  "details": "The first audio update already made it so a lot of people have to reupload avatars with audio because suddenly it is playing across the entire map or is inaudible. \nFor example, all of my 500 (!!!!) avatars have multiple audio sources, an engine sound and gun sound. The engine played across the entire map after the first update so I fix that and start updating them to linear audio sources. Now you roll out this new update and in the changelog it only mentions fixing something having to do with custom curves (which I did NOT use) and suddenly the gun sound audio source (logarithmic) is barely audible (minimum distance is 50!!!) when it could originally be heard just fine. Make up your mind with this audio BS already, some of us have wayyyy to many avatars to keep updating every other week to compensate for your poorly made updates that always manage to break more than they fix.",
